{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014hfLwLFxJyrSbsn3yzm68v","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test\n2\t  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic-register lane\n3\t   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n4\t\n5\t   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n6\t   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n7\t   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n8\t   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n9\t   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n10\t   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n11\t   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n12\t   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n13\t   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\"\n14\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n15\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n16\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n17\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n18\t            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n19\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n20\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n21\t            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n22\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n23\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n24\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n25\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n26\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n27\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]\n28\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n29\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n30\t            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n31\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n32\t            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n33\t\n34\t\n35\t;; ======================================================