*Refusal kind for F7.** I chose `:unsatisfied`/`:incomplete` with `:yin.k/stores`, which matches how\n  missing trees are reported. If the Architect's refusal table treats a store-of with no row as a\n  malformed carrier, the alternative is `:undecodable`. The change would be one line.\n- **`live-pcs` is public** only so the backward-jump property can be tested portably.\n- **Context pc semantics.** `at` is the pc the context resumes at (an act's or frame's pc, a closure's\n  entry), and it is included in the live set. If some context's `:pc` were ever the pc of an instruction\n  that already completed, including it would only make the check stricter, never looser.\n- The child's census is its own slot 7. Restore also builds each child's module stores from its own\n  rows, so the check and restore agree.\n"}}}
