{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxiqtWYSzvQakPBny2vH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both findings are fixed in the worktree. Kondo is clean and all the requested JVM lanes pass. Nothing is committed, and Node and Dart were not run. The report is at `collab/1792310000000-engineer-6b-fix2.report.md`.\n\n**F7 (High), missing module store accepted on lower.** Lower now checks, before any stream is attached, that every closure and frame names a module store carried by its own task. A child is judged only against its own stores, so a parent's store with the same key doesn't count. A missing store refuses as `:yin.k/unsatisfied`, discovery `:incomplete`, missing `{:yin.k/stores #{…}}`, which is the same shape as the missing-trees refusal. Each refusal test also asserts zero attaches:\n- **Codex's recipe:** with the task's module-store rows removed (`[:slots 7] []`), lower refuses. The intact carrier attaches once and `(f)` returns 42.\n- **Empty store present:** routing to a store that is present but empty lowers fine and returns 7. Removing its rows refuses.\n- **Frame path:** row 17, whose waiting frame is routed to a module store, refuses once that store's rows are removed.\n- **Child case:** row 10 with both parent and child routed to `scoped`. Removing only the child's rows refuses, even though the parent still carries a `scoped` store.\n\n**F6 (Medium), discharge checked dead code.** Discharge now checks only names reachable by control flow from each context's resume point. That includes jump targets and the bodies of any closure that reachable code can still construct. The rule for which environment and store answer a name is unchanged.\n- **Codex's `(if false ghost (next! …))` state** now transports. Source and receiver both complete with 73, with and without the unrelated module store, and also when the dead branch is a closure.\n- **Still refused:** a free read after the resume point, and a closure that can still be constructed after it.\n- **Backward jump:** the brief asked for an end-to-end case reached only through a backward jump, but well-formed vectors cannot contain one (`code/well-formed?` returns `:not-expression-structured`). So that test calls the reachability function directly on a hand-built vector. To make that portable I made it public (`rows/live-pcs`), because ClojureDart can't reach a private function from a test.\n\n**Attach-count law.** `bare-rows-match-the-reference` now checks, outside `laws`, that the corpus attaches a non-zero number of streams and that this equals the number of distinct stream identities. Codex's always-pass edit changes no behaviour, so no test can fail on that edit alone. Combined with a duplicate-attach bug, it now fails at the new check (and at the existing shared-tree test).\n\n**Mutants.** I ran all eleven on the quick harness and restored the sources byte-for-byte; every one was killed:\n- codex's union discharge;\n- dropping each of the four staged checks;\n- the always-pass law combined with duplicate attach;\n- five of my own: no reachability, reachability that ignores closure bodies, a plain \"pc ≥ resume\" filter, no store check, and a store check that skips frames.\n\nThe new F6 tests can't run against HEAD directly because `live-pcs` doesn't exist there. The \"no reachability\" mutant and codex's union mutant stand in for the old rule.\n\n**Verification:**\n\n| Lane | Tests | Assertions | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Harness + rows + audit, quick | 51 | 1,049 | 0 failures |\n| Same, `-i :slow` | 2 | 706 | 0 failures |\n| All `yin.vm.ucf.*` and `yin.vm.semantic-register.*` | 836 | 18,742 | 0 failures |\n\n**Decision for you:** the missing-store refusal kind. If the Architect's refusal table treats an unresolved store name as a malformed carrier rather than a missing dependency, it should be `:undecodable` instead; that's a one-line change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":775,"cache_read_input_tokens":118124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":775},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cf2c11fe-d429-4593-ac23-eac8d35e2316","uuid":"74e8e2b2-56e2-4670-bad2-1f4100266bb1","timestamp":"2026-10-12T17:17:01.850Z","request_id":"req_011CfxiqtFBHxCWhD96yaKdZ"}
